ok   a BEGIN left open inside a checkout is rolled back, and logged, when the connection comes back
ok   a BEGIN run and rolled back by hand is a clean check-in: no warning
ok   the connection goes back to the pool even when the leak warning cannot be logged
ok   a slot whose connection was closed is reopened on the next checkout
ok   a closed :memory: connection is an error on the next checkout, never a fresh database
ok   a pool that close_all shut down refuses every checkout instead of reopening
ok   abandon_transaction! leaves a clean connection alone and says so
ok   a StandardError rolls back, re-raises and leaves autocommit on
ok   a normal completion commits
ok   a nested transaction joins the outer one and an inner raise rolls everything back
